==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|stock-ticker}}, {{l|en|stockticker}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A device, used primarily in the 20th century, which printed prices and volumes of stock trades on paper tape as the data became available.
#* {{quote-book|en|The Boston Stock Exchange|author=Clarence W. Barron, Joseph Gregory Martin|year=1893|passage=... whose instruments are located directly on the floor of the Exchange, who transmit them instantly to the quotation companies, and in a few seconds the prices are carried by the '''stock-ticker''' into the brokers' office, the banks, banking houses...}}
# Any device or display showing price and volumes of stock trades as the data become available.

